# DO droplet → homebase `personal-tools/do` sync

**Canon notes:** `~/Repos/homebase/personal-tools/do/` (not this repo).  
Win: `C:\Users\ssofia\Repos\homebase\personal-tools\do\`  
**Primary:** `state.md`. Setup: `setup.md`.  
**Ops scripts:** `do/scripts/` (`books/` · `tls/` · `nginx/` · `archive/` — see `scripts/README.md`).

## When (same turn — do not leave stale)

Any change to the personal droplet `stellasis-personal-tools` / `152.42.203.20`, including:

- Volume attach / detach / resize / mount path / fstab
- Docker / Calibre-Web / Caddy / nginx / systemd services
- Disk free, RAM, firewall ports, HTTPS
- App path moves, new jobs on the box (Substack, ebooks, …)
- SSH host aliases or key path changes (also note in state Recall)
- New/moved DO runnable scripts under `do/scripts/`

## What to update

1. Edit `do/state.md`: Recall bullets · Shape ASCII · Inventory table · Next
2. Snapshot date at top if facts changed
3. Keep secrets out (no passwords / API keys)
4. If scripts layout changed → `do/scripts/README.md` + `do/README.md` one-liner

## Not this rule

- Everyday Substack scrape/content sync (`.notes/` / `.substack-sync/` in this repo)
- Azure / Contoso infra book
- Local ebook gather/scan (`Tools/ebook-cleanup`)
